cross all enhanced crops: (1) Tooth 16 shows a distinct distal-occlusal radiolucent defect breaching the enamel into dentin -- caries. (2) Tooth 27, the distally tilted upper-left second molar, shows a radiolucent halo at its occlusal/distal crown margin -- caries. (3) Tooth 36 shows a clear dark occlusal shadow in its crown -- caries. (4) Tooth 37 shows early but definite occlusal radiolucency adjacent to 36's lesion -- caries. (5) Tooth 48 shows a radiolucent rim around/beneath its occlusal restoration consistent with recurrent caries. All five regions were located via detector anchors plus verified nudged crops, cross-checked against contralateral mirrors, and confirmed on denoised, contrast-enhanced views.\", \"final_answer\": [{\"quadrant\": 1, \"tooth_position\": 6, \"diagnosis\": \"Caries\", \"confidence\": 0.86}, {\"quadrant\": 2, \"tooth_position\": 7, \"diagnosis\": \"Caries\", \"confidence\": 0.83}, {\"quadrant\": 3, \"tooth_position\": 6, \"diagnosis\": \"Caries\", \"confidence\": 0.88}, {\"quadrant\": 3, \"tooth_position\": 7, \"diagnosis\": \"Caries\", \"confidence\": 0.81}, {\"quadrant\": 4, \"tooth_position\": 8, \"diagnosis\": \"Caries\", \"confidence\": 0.78}]}", "parsed": {"thought": "Final confirmation review across all enhanced crops: (1) Tooth 16 shows a distinct distal-occlusal radiolucent defect breaching the enamel into dentin -- caries. (2) Tooth 27, the distally tilted upper-left second molar, shows a radiolucent halo at its occlusal/distal crown margin -- caries. (3) Tooth 36 shows a clear dark occlusal shadow in its crown -- caries. (4) Tooth 37 shows early but definite occlusal radiolucency adjacent to 36's lesion -- caries. (5) Tooth 48 shows a radiolucent rim around/beneath its occlusal restoration consistent with recurrent caries. All five regions were located via detector anchors plus verified nudged crops, cross-checked against contralateral mirrors, and confirmed on denoised, contrast-enhanced views.", "final_answer": [{"quadrant": 1, "tooth_position": 6, "diagnosis": "Caries", "confidence": 0.86}, {"quadrant": 2, "tooth_position": 7, "diagnosis": "Caries", "confidence": 0.83}, {"quadrant": 3, "tooth_position": 6, "diagnosis": "Caries", "confidence": 0.88}, {"quadrant": 3, "tooth_position": 7, "diagnosis": "Caries", "confidence": 0.81}, {"quadrant": 4, "tooth_position": 8, "diagnosis": "Caries", "confidence": 0.78}]}, "status": "rejected_final_answer"}, {"turn": 16, "raw_output": "{\"thought\": \"I need to formally run the detector on each of the five teeth I'm diagnosing rather than relying solely on derived boxes. Retrying locate_tooth for all five -- earlier failures may have been transient detector misses.\", \"tool_calls\": [{\"tool\": \"locate_tooth\", \"args\": {\"tooth\": 16}}, {\"tool\": \"locate_tooth\", \"args\": {\"tooth\": 27}}, {\"tool\": \"locate_tooth\", \"args\": {\"tooth\": 36}}, {\"tool\": \"locate_tooth\", \"args\": {\"tooth\": 37}}, {\"tool\": \"locate_tooth\", \"args\": {\"tooth\": 48}}]}", "parsed": {"thought": "I need to formally run the detector on each of the five teeth I'm diagnosing rather than relying solely on derived boxes. Retrying locate_tooth for all five -- earlier failures may have been transient detector misses.", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "locate_tooth", "args": {"tooth": 16}}, {"tool": "locate_tooth", "args": {"tooth": 27}}, {"tool": "locate_tooth", "args": {"tooth": 36}}, {"tool": "locate_tooth", "args": {"tooth": 37}}, {"tool": "locate_tooth", "args": {"tooth": 48}}]}, "status": "invalid_tool_format"}, {"turn": 17, "tool_calls_this_turn": [{"tool_name": "locate_tooth", "tool_args": {"tooth": 16}, "tool_ok": true}, {"tool_name": "locate_tooth", "tool_args": {"tooth": 27}, "tool_ok": true}, {"tool_name": "locate_tooth", "tool_args": {"tooth": 36}, "tool_ok": true}, {"tool_name": "locate_tooth", "tool_args": {"tooth": 37}, "tool_ok": true}], "status": "tool_executed"}, {"turn": 18, "tool_calls_this_turn": [{"tool_name": "zoom_crop", "tool_args": {"bbox": [